WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

0
00:00:03.759 --> 00:00:07.860
Congratulations to this entire slate

1
00:00:08.479 --> 00:00:10.100
to Governor-elect Phil Weiser,

2
00:00:10.239 --> 00:00:12.119
to Lieutenant Governor-elect Leslie Dahlf,

3
00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.199
to Jeff Bridges,

4
00:00:14.279 --> 00:00:15.479
to Jenna Griswold,

5
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.379
Amanda Gonzalez.

6
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.540
Congratulations to

7
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.600
my new colleagues in the delegation,

8
00:00:21.639 --> 00:00:22.350
Michael Bennett,

9
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.549
John Hickenlooper,

10
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:24.520
Joan Nagoose,

11
00:00:24.709 --> 00:00:25.329
Jason Crowe,

12
00:00:25.459 --> 00:00:26.420
Brittany Peterson.

13
00:00:28.079 --> 00:00:31.159
Incoming congressperson elect Mandy Ruinow.

14
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:35.729
And y'all were up everywhere else.

15
00:00:37.979 --> 00:00:38.880
I want to thank

16
00:00:39.299 --> 00:00:42.040
Congresswoman Diana DeGt for her 30

17
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.439
years of service to our city.

18
00:00:45.139 --> 00:00:46.700
She gave her career

19
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.450
to this district that I'm grateful to follow in her steps

20
00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:54.400
and the steps of the late great Congresswoman Pat Schroeder

21
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.000
as the 3rd woman

22
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.840
and the first black woman to represent

23
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.049
this incredible district.

24
00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:08.209
I'm a new member of this delegation and I'm also the youngest.

25
00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:09.470
I'm gonna.

26
00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.589
I'm gonna learn a lot from the people

27
00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:17.889
in this delegation who've been in these buildings longer than I have,

28
00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.470
and I plan to ask a lot of questions,

29
00:01:20.849 --> 00:01:24.949
but I'm also gonna stay true to what Denver sent me to do.

30
00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:30.550
Working people are tired and they are angry.

31
00:01:31.839 --> 00:01:34.809
Rent eats over half of our paychecks.

32
00:01:34.919 --> 00:01:36.849
Energy bills keep going up.

33
00:01:37.089 --> 00:01:39.110
Premiums go up every year,

34
00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:43.209
and no one trusts Washington to get anything done.

35
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.059
We earn that trust back

36
00:01:47.199 --> 00:01:49.940
by showing them who we work for

37
00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.379
and by delivering

38
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.660
so let's be clear

39
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.760
about what this party believes

40
00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.500
we believe that everyone deserves a home they can afford.

41
00:02:02.769 --> 00:02:04.900
We believe that no one

42
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.639
should go bankrupt because they got sick.

43
00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:09.788
We believe your vote

44
00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.830
should count just as much as a billionaire's.

45
00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:18.330
And we believe that Colorado belongs to everyone here whether

46
00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.449
you crossed the border or the border crossed you.

47
00:02:24.589 --> 00:02:28.429
I will not pretend that the work ahead will be easy.

48
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.770
The future that we are reaching for is vast,

49
00:02:33.369 --> 00:02:37.410
even more vast than the injustices that it is meant to answer.

50
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.130
Healthcare as a right,

51
00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.399
a home as a foundation,

52
00:02:42.649 --> 00:02:43.710
not a reward.

53
00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.350
Health care as a right,

54
00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.089
a home as a foundation,

55
00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.360
a government that answers to the voters,

56
00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.750
not the donors.

57
00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:56.410
These are not just policies to be passed

58
00:02:56.789 --> 00:02:59.369
but promises to be made,

59
00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:03.089
and promises of this size are not kept

60
00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.800
in a single moment

61
00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:10.919
but over years of labor by many hands against fierce resistance.

62
00:03:11.389 --> 00:03:13.330
Look at how hard they worked

63
00:03:13.509 --> 00:03:15.229
to repeal Obamacare.

64
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:18.449
We must be fierce in our resistance.

65
00:03:20.509 --> 00:03:22.800
But I take comfort in knowing,

66
00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.899
in remembering who we are.

67
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.320
We live in the legacy of those who looked at

68
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.500
the moon and decided it was close enough to touch,

69
00:03:32.039 --> 00:03:36.990
those who crossed oceans to break the back of fascism and hatred,

70
00:03:37.399 --> 00:03:39.800
those who turned prairie and steel

71
00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:43.119
into the greatest economy the world has ever known.

72
00:03:44.419 --> 00:03:47.360
None of that was handed to us.

73
00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.789
It was willed into being

74
00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:54.800
by ordinary people who refused to accept the world as it was

75
00:03:54.979 --> 00:03:58.279
and decided instead to fight for a world that could be.

76
00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:04.419
And the crisis before us for all its weight

77
00:04:04.619 --> 00:04:06.520
is no act of nature.

78
00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.759
It is the sum of choices made

79
00:04:09.059 --> 00:04:10.660
by a powerful few

80
00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.199
in rooms most of us will never see.

81
00:04:13.779 --> 00:04:15.270
But what was chosen

82
00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.959
can be unchosen.

83
00:04:17.339 --> 00:04:18.488
What was built

84
00:04:18.738 --> 00:04:20.160
can be rebuilt,

85
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:26.399
and there is no force on earth more powerful than a people who have finally decided

86
00:04:26.619 --> 00:04:27.119
they

87
00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.859
deserve better.

88
00:04:31.829 --> 00:04:34.940
Who here thinks that we deserve better.

89
00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:39.579
All right,

90
00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:40.950
then let's get to work.

91
00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:41.950
Because

92
00:04:42.459 --> 00:04:43.709
when we fight.

93
00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.339
When we fight.

94
00:04:47.109 --> 00:04:48.690
When we fight.

95
00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:50.450
Damn straight.

96
00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:51.190
Let's get to work,

97
00:04:51.269 --> 00:04:51.750
Colorado.

98
00:04:51.829 --> 00:04:52.510
Thank you.

99
00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.350
Please welcome Congressman Brittany Peterson.

